<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="Adobe XMP Core 5.6-c017 91.164464, 2020/06/15-10:20:05        ">
   <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
      <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
            xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
            xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/"
            xmlns:pdf="http://ns.adobe.com/pdf/1.3/"
            xmlns:xmpMM="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/"
            xmlns:illustrator="http://ns.adobe.com/illustrator/1.0/">
         <dc:format>application/pdf</dc:format>
         <dc:title>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">NCP1230 - PWM Controller, Fixed Frequency, Current Mode</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:title>
         <dc:creator>
            <rdf:Seq>
               <rdf:li>ON Semiconductor</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Seq>
         </dc:creator>
         <dc:description>
            <rdf:Alt>
               <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The NCP1230 represents a major leap towards achieving low&#xD;&#xA;standby power in mediumâˆ’toâˆ’high power Switchedâˆ’Mode Power&#xD;&#xA;Supplies such as notebook adapters, offâˆ’line battery chargers and&#xD;&#xA;consumer electronics equipment. Housed in a compact 8âˆ’pin package&#xD;&#xA;(SOICâˆ’8, SOICâˆ’7, or PDIPâˆ’7), the NCP1230 contains all needed&#xD;&#xA;control functionality to build a rugged and efficient power supply. The&#xD;&#xA;NCP1230 is a current mode controller with internal ramp&#xD;&#xA;compensation. Among the unique features offered by the NCP1230 is&#xD;&#xA;an event management scheme that can disable the frontâˆ’end PFC&#xD;&#xA;circuit during standby, thus reducing the no load power consumption.&#xD;&#xA;The NCP1230 itself goes into cycle skipping at light loads while&#xD;&#xA;limiting peak current (to 25% of nominal peak) so that no acoustic&#xD;&#xA;noise is generated. The NCP1230 has a highâˆ’voltage startup circuit&#xD;&#xA;that eliminates external components and reduces power consumption.&#xD;&#xA;The NCP1230 also features an internal latching function that can be&#xD;&#xA;used for OVP protection. This latch is triggered by pulling the CS pin&#xD;&#xA;above 3.0 V and can only be reset by pulling VCC to ground. True&#xD;&#xA;overload protection, internal 2.5 ms softâˆ’start, internal leading edge&#xD;&#xA;blanking, internal frequency dithering for low EMI are some of the&#xD;&#xA;other important features offered by the NCP1230.</rdf:li>
            </rdf:Alt>
         </dc:description>
         <xmp:CreateDate>2015-05-05T17:58:46-07:00</xmp:CreateDate>
         <xmp:CreatorTool>BroadVision, Inc.</xmp:CreatorTool>
         <xmp:ModifyDate>2020-09-29T09:48:07+02:00</xmp:ModifyDate>
         <xmp:MetadataDate>2020-09-29T09:48:07+02:00</xmp:MetadataDate>
         <pdf:Producer>Acrobat Distiller 10.0.0 (Windows)</pdf:Producer>
